{
  "id": "Compound::DB06684 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Vilazodone, Desvenlafaxine, and Levomilnacipran are all antidepressants that share a common ancestry as organic aromatic compounds and are classified as antidepressants. The evidence suggests that Vilazodone may influence Cyp3a4 through a chain of interactions involving these compounds. Specifically, Vilazodone is linked to Hemorrhage Abnormal and Orgasm Abnormal, both of which are caused by Desvenlafaxine, which binds to Cyp3a4. Similarly, Vilazodone is associated with Hemorrhage Abnormal, which is caused by Levomilnacipran, which also binds to Cyp3a4. This indicates that Vilazodone may exert its effects on Cyp3a4 through the indirect pathway of these antidepressants. The shared mechanism of binding to Cyp3a4 across different antidepressants suggests a potential role for Cyp3a4 in the metabolism of these drugs, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
